{"t": 1794117206.7150688, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "CI fix for the red main pipeline (pipeline #8812)\n\nFailure: job `test:contract` failed in `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`:\n  assert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\n  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n\nRoot cause: `billing/invoice.py` interpolated the raw sequence number, so no zero-padding was applied. The contract test documents the Finance ERP import requirement (FIN-77): the sequence part must be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\nFix applied to `billing/invoice.py`:\n  - return f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"\n  + return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n\n`:06d` is a minimum width, so values above 999999 still render in full and are not truncated. Verified locally:\n  invoice_number(2026, 42) -> INV-2026-000042\n  invoice_number(2026, 7)  -> INV-2026-000007\n  invoice_number(2026, 1234567) -> INV-2026-1234567\n\nFor this MR (ERP v2): please make sure the ERP v2 invoice formatter keeps the same 6-digit zero-padded sequence, otherwise the contract test will go red again after merge.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
